1
00:01:22,462 --> 00:01:28,945
Tonight we'll talk about the famous, nightly patrols

2
00:01:29,001 --> 00:01:32,213
 of the Ameer Ul Mo'mineen(أمير المؤمنين) Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه.

3
00:01:36,746 --> 00:01:39,524
These are some of the most amazing stories of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

4
00:01:41,457 --> 00:01:47,670
The Khalifah(خليفه) going around at night on patrols,

5
00:01:49,872 --> 00:01:55,104
to make sure that his Ummah(امة) is fine and well,

6
00:01:57,172 --> 00:02:00,973
to make sure that they are happy, to make sure that they are content.

7
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:16,183
And he would take along with him people like Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضى الله عنه.

8
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:22,281
He would take with him, his servant Salim(سالم),

9
00:02:24,054 --> 00:02:26,846
he would take with him his servant Yarfah(يرفه).

10
00:02:28,132 --> 00:02:33,195
He had different people accompany him on these journeys.

11
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:53,660
One night Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, saw some guests in the Masjid(مسجد).

12
00:02:55,304 --> 00:02:56,677
These were travelers

13
00:02:57,812 --> 00:03:03,323
and the travelers would sometimes stay at Al-Masjid-Al-Nabwi(ألمسجد ألنبوي) they would sleep on Al-Musallah(مصله).

14
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:06,920
The Masjid(مسجد) was open there's no lock pad.

15
00:03:08,388 --> 00:03:10,462
What are you going to steal from "Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد ألنبوي)"

16
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:18,539
 no speakers, no microphones, no rugs, so it's open.

17
00:03:20,746 --> 00:03:25,658
These travelers Abiree Sabeel(عا برى سبيل) would spend their night in the Musallah(مصله).

18
00:03:28,850 --> 00:03:33,380
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه told Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف),

19
00:03:33,989 --> 00:03:37,384
would you like to join me, so we could guard them this evening.

20
00:03:39,599 --> 00:03:44,308
Now, they have belongings, so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to guard them.

21
00:03:47,746 --> 00:03:49,262
And what can you say about such a thing?

22
00:03:49,286 --> 00:03:51,984
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) guarding these travelers.

23
00:03:52,676 --> 00:03:57,377
You can say it's humbleness, you can say it's a sense of responsibility,

24
00:03:57,741 --> 00:04:01,474
you can say it's love for Muslims, you call it whatever you want.

25
00:04:04,747 --> 00:04:06,579
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is telling another man

26
00:04:06,603 --> 00:04:09,082
who was among the10 who were given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة)

27
00:04:09,106 --> 00:04:11,874
You know Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) and their likes,

28
00:04:12,453 --> 00:04:16,367
they've already been given the Bushra Bil-Jannah(بشرا بالجنة).

29
00:04:16,392 --> 00:04:19,064
They are among the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة),

30
00:04:19,291 --> 00:04:20,646
so why not just sit at home.

31
00:04:22,416 --> 00:04:25,674
Why do you have to go through all of this hassle and difficulty,

32
00:04:25,714 --> 00:04:28,753
you already have that badge of honor.

33
00:04:31,528 --> 00:04:33,883
Just do your Salah(صلاة) do your Ibadaat(عبادات) and that's enough,

34
00:04:35,067 --> 00:04:39,345
you're Khalifah(خليفه) and you're guarding and you're spending the hours of the night

35
00:04:39,369 --> 00:04:41,915
these people are sleeping and you're guarding them.

36
00:04:45,522 --> 00:04:47,299
Abdur Rahman bin Auf (عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said: Yes! Definitely.

37
00:04:51,457 --> 00:04:59,399
So, Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, he hears a child crying, an infant was crying.

38
00:05:01,195 --> 00:05:05,129
He is crying for some time, so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) goes to the mother and says,

39
00:05:05,153 --> 00:05:07,340
اِتَّقِى اللهَ وَ اَحْسَنِ اِلَى هَذِا اصَّبِيْحََ

40
00:05:07,774 --> 00:05:14,215
 Fear Allah and take care of your child and then he leaves.

41
00:05:14,582 --> 00:05:18,118
The child is carry on crying, he is crying again, He is crying again.

42
00:05:18,312 --> 00:05:22,718
Towards the end of the night, he goes to her and say, what kind of mother are you?

43
00:05:22,743 --> 00:05:27,694
You are an evil mother, your child has been crying since the beginning of the night.

44
00:05:29,905 --> 00:05:35,831
She said: I'm trying to wean him, but he doesn't want to eat the food.

45
00:05:37,335 --> 00:05:39,839
This child still wants to breastfeed

46
00:05:40,398 --> 00:05:45,253
and his mother is trying to convince him to eat, rather than breastfeed.

47
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:52,080
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Why are you trying to wean him, how old is he?

48
00:05:53,693 --> 00:05:56,916
She said: He's a few months old.

49
00:05:58,990 --> 00:06:00,008
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

50
00:06:00,093 --> 00:06:00,493
 الله اتقى,

51
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:02,020
Why are you trying to wean him then?

52
00:06:04,665 --> 00:06:10,337
Because the complete period of breastfeeding is how long! Two years,

53
00:06:11,546 --> 00:06:13,673
so he said: Why are you trying to wean him.?

54
00:06:14,591 --> 00:06:21,933
She said: "Because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) does not start paying them, until they are weaned."

55
00:06:23,377 --> 00:06:25,919
Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) does not give the handouts

56
00:06:26,564 --> 00:06:31,482
except when the child reaches Al-Fitaar(ألفطار).

57
00:06:33,602 --> 00:06:39,618
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Woe to you, son of Al-Khattab(الخطاب),

58
00:06:40,266 --> 00:06:41,067
What have you done?

59
00:06:44,268 --> 00:06:53,186
And he then in Salat-Ul-Fajar(صلاة الفجر) he was so taken back by what happened

60
00:06:54,893 --> 00:06:57,884
people could not recognize his Qira'ah(قراءة) because of his crying,

61
00:06:59,187 --> 00:07:02,388
he was weeping so bad they couldn’t recognize his recitation.

62
00:07:04,812 --> 00:07:09,829
And then he immediately after Salat-Ul-Fajar(صلاة الفجر) issues an order, a government order

63
00:07:11,542 --> 00:07:15,902
to the mothers around the Muslim world, he sent this message all over, he said;

64
00:07:16,295 --> 00:07:20,892
Don't wean your children too early, because from now on,

65
00:07:21,263 --> 00:07:24,684
you will receive a handout the day your child is born.

66
00:07:27,921 --> 00:07:30,683
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: How many children have I killed?

67
00:07:31,124 --> 00:07:33,887
يا عمر اِتَّقِى اللهَ كَمْ قَتَلْتَ مِنْ اَطْفَالِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ

68
00:07:34,499 --> 00:07:36,406
How many children have been killed because of you?

69
00:07:38,363 --> 00:07:40,260
What is Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saying, who did he killed?

70
00:07:40,386 --> 00:07:41,494
Which children did he kill?

71
00:07:44,699 --> 00:07:48,234
This is a favor that he's doing to the people, he's giving them these handouts.

72
00:07:49,786 --> 00:07:54,040
But he was so emotional because of what he saw,

73
00:07:54,080 --> 00:08:01,934
and he was so upset with the law that state that they should be given this money at the age of two.

74
00:08:03,313 --> 00:08:09,489
He considered that he has harmed the Muslim infants

75
00:08:09,513 --> 00:08:13,944
because their mothers are trying to wean them sooner to get the handouts.

76
00:08:16,244 --> 00:08:22,468
Can you think about such a government you don't pay any taxes

77
00:08:23,174 --> 00:08:25,576
and you still receive handouts from the government.

78
00:08:27,213 --> 00:08:33,146
Ya'ani(يعني) now governments are ripping their people off, taking 30% in taxes or more

79
00:08:36,367 --> 00:08:37,750
and they give you nothing.

80
00:08:39,922 --> 00:08:43,878
Supposedly they take this money to offer you services.

81
00:08:43,974 --> 00:08:45,544
Where does all of that money go?

82
00:08:45,669 --> 00:08:47,526
So much money, Where does it go?

83
00:08:49,753 --> 00:08:52,432
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab( عمر ابن الخطاب), first of all, in the Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

84
00:08:52,457 --> 00:08:55,459
there was nothing called the Zariba(ضريبة) no taxes at all.

85
00:08:55,866 --> 00:08:57,999
They didn't know the concept of taxes.

86
00:08:59,012 --> 00:09:02,550
This concept of Al-Makoos(المكوس), was something that existed

87
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,238
among the Romans and the Persians.

88
00:09:04,775 --> 00:09:07,331
In Khilafah(خِلَافَه) Al-Islamia no Al-Makoos(المكوس).

89
00:09:10,625 --> 00:09:14,809
All what would be taken from you is Zakat(زكواة) if you are capable of giving it

90
00:09:18,368 --> 00:09:23,007
and Ushur(أشور), this is something that was started by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and that's like customs

91
00:09:23,641 --> 00:09:28,164
 for businessmen who are coming from outside Al-Khilafah(خِلَافَه), they would pay customs,

92
00:09:28,245 --> 00:09:30,141
and we'll talk about that later on.

93
00:09:32,282 --> 00:09:34,073
But the government gives you money

94
00:09:34,751 --> 00:09:38,444
and the moment your child is born you're gonna start receiving those handouts.

95
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:54,986
During one of his patrols, he passes by this house and you know in those days

96
00:09:55,254 --> 00:10:02,264
the house didn't have a front yard in the backyard, and a huge garden and soundproof walls,

97
00:10:03,622 --> 00:10:08,818
 these were very modest buildings, mud bricks and

98
00:10:09,131 --> 00:10:15,281
the house is basically composed of a few rooms and that's it, not very high.

99
00:10:18,069 --> 00:10:22,211
The house of Rasool Allah ﷺ one could touch the ceiling with your hand as Al-Hasan Al-Basri(الحسن البصرى) said.

100
00:10:26,552 --> 00:10:30,100
So, you could hear what's happening inside these houses.

101
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:35,209
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is walking and he hears a woman and this was very late at night.

102
00:10:37,953 --> 00:10:40,494
This woman was reciting lines of poetry.

103
00:10:41,586 --> 00:10:44,754
تَطَاوَلَ هَذَالَّيْلَ تَسْرِيْ كَوَاكِبْه

104
00:10:44,778 --> 00:10:48,181
وَأَرَّقَنِيْ أَلَّا ضَجِيْحٌ أُلَاعِبُه

105
00:10:50,624 --> 00:10:52,585
The lines go on and in the end , she says,

106
00:10:52,642 --> 00:10:58,257
وَلَكِنَنِيْ أَخْشَى رَقِيْبًأ مُوْكَلًا بِأَنْفُسِنَا لَا يَفْتُرْ اَلدَّهَرْ كَاتِبُه

107
00:11:00,636 --> 00:11:04,062
Basically, this woman was a wife of one of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

108
00:11:05,347 --> 00:11:08,968
her husband was away for a very long time and she was feeling very lonely.

109
00:11:09,612 --> 00:11:12,105
She has no children, she staying at home alone.

110
00:11:13,127 --> 00:11:15,619
So, she was reciting these lines of poetry.

111
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:19,009
The first line, what it means is,

112
00:11:19,444 --> 00:11:23,279
this night is very, very long, and I have no companion to be with me.

113
00:11:24,161 --> 00:11:28,178
And then she goes on to say that if it wasn't for Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

114
00:11:28,581 --> 00:11:31,794
I would have been with another man,

115
00:11:33,068 --> 00:11:37,096
so basically, she's saying, if it wasn't for Allah, I would have committed Haram(حرام).

116
00:11:38,144 --> 00:11:40,967
And then she said, but because I fear Allahعَزّوجَلّ

117
00:11:41,347 --> 00:11:44,770
and because there's an eye that is watching me all the time.

118
00:11:45,303 --> 00:11:50,157
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has appointed two angels to you, one on the right and one on the left.

119
00:11:50,566 --> 00:11:55,108
She said: If it wasn't for that I would have, had the companion with me now.

120
00:11:56,883 --> 00:11:58,598
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه  said;

121
00:11:58,656 --> 00:12:00,420
"يرحمك الله"

122
00:12:00,665 --> 00:12:03,432
May Allahعَزّوجَلّ have mercy on you.

123
00:12:03,523 --> 00:12:05,443
He wasn't speaking to her he was making the Dua(دُعَا) for her

124
00:12:06,883 --> 00:12:10,744
and then he goes to his daughter Hafsah(حفصه), Umm Ul-Mo'mineen(أم المؤمنين),

125
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:16,035
and he knocks and Hafsah(حفصه) said: Oh my father,

126
00:12:16,059 --> 00:12:19,449
Why did you come in this late hour, it must be something very urgent.

127
00:12:20,444 --> 00:12:25,845
So, he comes in and he says: For how long can a woman wait for her husband?

128
00:12:25,869 --> 00:12:27,732
How long can she stay alone?

129
00:12:28,650 --> 00:12:30,444
How long will her patience last?

130
00:12:31,504 --> 00:12:35,879
So Hafsah(حفصه) said: One month, two months, three months,

131
00:12:36,225 --> 00:12:39,525
 and then after four months her patience runs out.

132
00:12:40,879 --> 00:12:43,563
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) immediately issues his orders

133
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:49,602
that no Muslim soldier should stay away from his wife more than four months.

134
00:12:52,643 --> 00:12:56,059
So, the rotation is four months

135
00:12:57,222 --> 00:13:01,114
you know, even today with the fast modes of transportation,

136
00:13:01,588 --> 00:13:05,585
they don't do four months services, six months a year.

137
00:13:07,189 --> 00:13:11,177
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: If that's how long she can wait.

138
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:17,312
We don't want our sisters to wait longer than that,

139
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:21,823
if four months is the limit then they should come back after four months.

140
00:13:26,463 --> 00:13:31,177
But there was a problem, many of those soldiers didn't want to come back.

141
00:13:35,165 --> 00:13:40,934
You know, now soldiers are crying, we want to go back to mom and dad.

142
00:13:42,048 --> 00:13:43,563
I want to go back to my girlfriend.

143
00:13:44,142 --> 00:13:46,876
They are weeping they are crying, you see them on TV, they're crying all the time.

144
00:13:53,035 --> 00:13:56,168
But these who were Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) some of them didn't want to go back.

145
00:13:57,224 --> 00:14:00,273
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had to force them, he sent some orders.

146
00:14:00,918 --> 00:14:06,558
He said: You either go back or I'm going to give you an exemption

147
00:14:07,773 --> 00:14:12,960
but you have to give Nafaqa(نفقه) to your wife, sufficient money

148
00:14:13,234 --> 00:14:17,323
you have to provide her with sufficient money, so that she wouldn't be in any need,

149
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:20,340
otherwise you divorce.

150
00:14:22,158 --> 00:14:23,507
Otherwise you divorce.

151
00:14:25,963 --> 00:14:34,802
So, you see that these are teachings that show the care that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had for the Muslim family.

152
00:14:36,655 --> 00:14:43,630
How eager he was to make sure that men are happy, women are happy, children are happy.

153
00:14:45,267 --> 00:14:48,077
So, four months was the maximum time

154
00:14:50,903 --> 00:15:01,356
but what happened was, in the time of Umar(عُمَر) because now the land that was conquered was expanding

155
00:15:02,474 --> 00:15:05,538
and it was getting further away from Makkah and Madina.

156
00:15:07,375 --> 00:15:14,246
They were starting to establish towns up north and these were military towns

157
00:15:15,138 --> 00:15:20,957
like Al-Basra(ألبصرة), Al-Kufa(الكوفه), Al-Mosul(الموصل), Al-Fustat(ألفستات), Al-Jeza(ألجيزة).

158
00:15:21,309 --> 00:15:24,590
All of  these were towns that were founded my Muslims.

159
00:15:25,721 --> 00:15:28,287
Baghdad(بغداد) was later on founded by Al-Abbasieen(ألعباسيين).

160
00:15:29,314 --> 00:15:35,241
So, you can see that the most important towns in Iraq were actually founded in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

161
00:15:35,362 --> 00:15:39,224
Al-Kufa(الكوفه), Al-Basra(ألبصرة), Al-Mosul(الموصل), these are some of the most famous towns in Iraq.

162
00:15:39,619 --> 00:15:42,743
These were initially military towns.

163
00:15:45,179 --> 00:15:53,786
To make it easy on the soldiers, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he has sent orders to his commanders

164
00:15:54,574 --> 00:16:02,361
to build new towns, so that the Muslims can bring their families in, and they set base there.

165
00:16:03,057 --> 00:16:08,608
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) these towns became, so important and so vibrant

166
00:16:09,661 --> 00:16:14,102
that the weight of the Muslim world was actually in those towns

167
00:16:14,716 --> 00:16:19,678
and they became more important commercially and politically, then Makkah Madina.

168
00:16:20,609 --> 00:16:23,849
Obviously Makkah and Madina retain their religious importance

169
00:16:24,336 --> 00:16:28,945
but politically and commercially these other towns picked up.

170
00:16:29,296 --> 00:16:31,995
So, you see that in the time of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

171
00:16:32,256 --> 00:16:36,172
he actually moved the capital of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) from Al-Madina to Al-Kufa(ألكوفه).

172
00:16:37,725 --> 00:16:41,233
They were becoming the center of the Muslim world

173
00:16:42,056 --> 00:16:43,961
and then Damascus, and Jerusalem

174
00:16:44,281 --> 00:16:48,683
and Al-Fustat(ألفستات) which grew later to become a Cairo.

175
00:16:49,841 --> 00:16:54,245
But it was because of Al-Ghazoo(ألغزؤ) because of these military expeditions

176
00:16:54,606 --> 00:17:00,186
that these towns were founded and that's what gave them prominence and importance.

177
00:17:00,558 --> 00:17:05,223
So, now they were moving with their families and going up north to these lands of Ribat(رباط).

178
00:17:06,652 --> 00:17:15,428
So, you can see that how the Ghazoo(غزؤ) was really the central theme with the Khulafah رضي الله عنهم

179
00:17:15,746 --> 00:17:20,904
and you would find that everything revolves around it even commerce, business, building towns everything.

180
00:17:31,552 --> 00:17:34,854
In another occasion, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) heard this woman

181
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:40,444
also apparently a wife of one of the soldiers,

182
00:17:41,069 --> 00:17:44,476
who was absent it was one line poetry. She said:

183
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:50,102
هَلْ مِنْ سَبِيْلٍ إِلَى خَمْرٍ فَأَشْرَبُهَا
هَلْ مِنْ سَبِيْلٍ إِلَى نَصَرْ بِنْ حَجَّاجِ

184
00:17:51,594 --> 00:17:56,263
Is there any way for me to get hold of a cup of wine to drink,

185
00:17:56,685 --> 00:18:00,880
and is there any way of me to get in touch with Nasr Bin Hajjaj(نصر بن حجاج).

186
00:18:02,287 --> 00:18:04,241
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not like these words.

