Umar(عُمَر) said: You heard that, he said: Yes! I did.

739
01:05:05,379 --> 01:05:07,937
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: And I didn't know about it?

740
01:05:10,205 --> 01:05:13,443
Yes! Because I was busy doing business in the market place.

741
01:05:15,267 --> 01:05:20,381
And what kept me from hearing these Ahadith(احاديث) is trade "business".

742
01:05:21,045 --> 01:05:23,619
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) blamed himself for not knowing this,

743
01:05:24,013 --> 01:05:26,503
even though everybody else knew it.

744
01:05:28,854 --> 01:05:33,106
But this is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم) and also in a Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ).

745
01:05:34,484 --> 01:05:35,926
But this shows you something that,

746
01:05:36,052 --> 01:05:39,489
the Ahadith(احاديث) were not all known by all of the Sahabah(صحابه),

747
01:05:40,184 --> 01:05:43,043
this Sahabi(صحابي) would know some Ahadith(احاديث), another Sahabi(صحابي) would know some Ahadith(احاديث).

748
01:05:43,107 --> 01:05:44,718
So, their knowledge complements each other.

749
01:05:45,369 --> 01:05:49,733
Number two, it shows you that the way of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was strict in the narration of Hadith(حديث).

750
01:05:50,174 --> 01:05:54,250
He didn't want people narrating a Hadith(حديث) unless there's a confirmation,

751
01:05:54,775 --> 01:05:57,954
there's a witness because you could forget, you can make a mistake,

752
01:05:58,256 --> 01:06:00,259
you think that it was said, when it wasn't.

753
01:06:00,552 --> 01:06:03,500
That's the nature of the human mind.

754
01:06:03,991 --> 01:06:07,288
I mean Adam عليه السّلام, you know the story between him and Dawood(داؤد),

755
01:06:08,472 --> 01:06:14,971
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Adam عليه السّلام was presented with his children, all of them.

756
01:06:15,839 --> 01:06:18,093
Adam عليه السّلام saw all of his children

757
01:06:20,097 --> 01:06:27,139
and they had light on them, according to their righteousness,

758
01:06:28,194 --> 01:06:33,362
so he saw one of his children and he liked him, he said: Who is he?

759
01:06:33,994 --> 01:06:35,935
They said: This is Nabi Ullah(نبي الله) Dawood(داؤد)!

760
01:06:37,299 --> 01:06:38,508
Now all of these are his children.

761
01:06:38,873 --> 01:06:40,049
So, they said, this is Nabi Ullah(نبي الله) Dawood(داؤد),

762
01:06:41,965 --> 01:06:44,400
Adam عليه السّلام said: How long will Dawood(داؤد) live?

763
01:06:44,678 --> 01:06:47,839
They said: He's gonna live 60 years.

764
01:06:48,793 --> 01:06:53,843
Adam عليه السّلام said: Why don't you give him 40 years from my life.

765
01:06:55,782 --> 01:06:58,312
So, that he would have hundred years to live.

766
01:06:58,909 --> 01:07:01,693
So, they said: It's Maktoob(مكتبوب),

767
01:07:01,892 --> 01:07:05,739
It's written that you are giving him 40 years of your life.

768
01:07:08,267 --> 01:07:12,061
Tayyeb(طيب), when the angel of death came to Adam عليه السّلام claiming his Soul.

769
01:07:13,440 --> 01:07:19,825
Adam عليه السّلام said: No! It's not my time yet, I still have 40 years in my life

770
01:07:21,606 --> 01:07:26,542
because he was told that he's going to live for this time he gave 40 years to Dawood(داؤد).

771
01:07:27,005 --> 01:07:29,444
So, the angel of death was 40 years early.

772
01:07:30,682 --> 01:07:35,394
He said: No! I didn't say that.

773
01:07:35,647 --> 01:07:37,378
I didn't give Dawood(داؤد) anything.

774
01:07:41,153 --> 01:07:42,364
The angel said: Yes! You did.

775
01:07:42,535 --> 01:07:43,512
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

776
01:07:43,610 --> 01:07:49,986
 وَنُسِّيَ آدَمُ فَنُسِّيَتْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُ 'فَجَحَدَ آدَمُ ، فَجَحَدَتْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُ ، وَخَطِئَ آدَمُ فَخَطِئَتْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُ

777
01:07:50,011 --> 01:07:50,718
And this Hadith(حديث) is Sahih(صحيح).

778
01:07:51,051 --> 01:07:56,572
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:  Adam(آدم) Forgot, and that's why his children forget.

779
01:07:58,030 --> 01:08:01,511
And Adam(آدم) refused and that's why his children of refuse.

780
01:08:02,967 --> 01:08:08,287
He refused to accept the fact that he has actually, he did actually give Dawood 40 years of his life.

781
01:08:08,327 --> 01:08:09,418
 He refused to accept that.

782
01:08:10,102 --> 01:08:11,203
Why? Because he forgot.

783
01:08:11,528 --> 01:08:13,901
And that's the nature in us, we forget, you could forget.

784
01:08:16,964 --> 01:08:20,251
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was asking the Sahabah(صحابه): what should one do,

785
01:08:21,253 --> 01:08:25,101
when the lose the major Taharah(طهارة) and there's no water around?

786
01:08:26,988 --> 01:08:30,039
You know, it's not the Wadhoo(وضؤ) that you lost, you lost the major Taharah(طهارة).

787
01:08:32,098 --> 01:08:35,292
Ammar Bin Yasir(عماربن ياسر) said: You, make Tayammum(تيمم).

788
01:08:37,421 --> 01:08:39,415
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Where did you get that from?

789
01:08:39,460 --> 01:08:44,320
Ammar Bin Yasir(عماربن ياسر) Said: You forgot when me and you were traveling together?

790
01:08:46,744 --> 01:08:53,429
And I lost my Taharah(طهارة).

791
01:08:54,463 --> 01:08:59,832
And there was no water, so I rolled my body in the dirt like an animal would.

792
01:09:00,816 --> 01:09:04,410
And then we went back to Rasool Allah ﷺ me and you, and we asked him about it.

793
01:09:04,435 --> 01:09:06,914
He said: It was enough and sufficient for you to make Tayammum(تيمم).

794
01:09:07,598 --> 01:09:10,079
Do you remember that? Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: No! I forgot about it.

795
01:09:11,054 --> 01:09:14,216
This was a Hadith(حديث) that was mentioned in front of Umar(عُمَر) and he forgot about it.

796
01:09:15,710 --> 01:09:18,921
Ammar Bin Yasir(عماربن ياسر) Said: Well, if you don't want me to mention this Hadith(حديث),

797
01:09:18,945 --> 01:09:19,817
I won't mention it.

798
01:09:20,342 --> 01:09:22,792
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: No! Go ahead and mention it.

799
01:09:23,413 --> 01:09:26,562
But after there was a witness to say that, this actually happened.

800
01:09:31,425 --> 01:09:36,272
Therefore brothers, we learn from this, we should be careful in narrating Ahadith(احاديث)

801
01:09:37,440 --> 01:09:40,629
and we should make sure that, the Ahadith(احاديث) that we're following are authentic,

802
01:09:41,383 --> 01:09:48,154
you know, we don't want to be fooled by following Ahadith(احاديث) that Rasool Allah ﷺ did not say.

803
01:09:48,206 --> 01:09:51,160
 I mean, why should I do something, when Rasool Allah ﷺ did not tell me to do it

804
01:09:51,679 --> 01:09:54,490
and I'm wasting my time doing something that is not expected from me.

805
01:09:54,978 --> 01:10:00,096
I could use that time wisely by doing something that Allah wants me to do.

806
01:10:01,471 --> 01:10:03,933
Don't think that you're a good Muslim by following everything you hear.

807
01:10:05,960 --> 01:10:17,051
You need to make sure that the information that you're following is verified and true, he said;

808
01:10:17,153 --> 01:10:23,252
تَفَكَّه’ قَبْلَ اَنْتَ سُوْدُوْفَتَمْنَعَكُمْ اَنَفَ مِنَّ التَّعَّلُّمْ فَتَعِيْشُوْجُهَالَه’

809
01:10:23,929 --> 01:10:27,905
He said: Learn before you're put in positions of leadership

810
01:10:29,154 --> 01:10:32,928
because then your pride will prevent you from learning.

811
01:10:33,439 --> 01:10:36,899
So, you will live the rest of your life in a state of ignorance.

812
01:10:38,298 --> 01:10:41,937
Learn when you're young, learn when you're young, don't wait.

813
01:10:42,449 --> 01:10:45,908
because the older you become, the more senior you become,

814
01:10:46,379 --> 01:10:51,213
the more you are seen in a high level and you are seen as a leader

815
01:10:51,527 --> 01:10:53,716
and when you are seen as a leader,

816
01:10:53,912 --> 01:10:57,192
you wouldn't go and sit under the knees of the scholars to learn,

817
01:10:57,952 --> 01:11:02,858
and you wouldn't go around asking the people who are younger than you about knowledge

818
01:11:03,733 --> 01:11:07,534
that's not the case with everyone many people are humbled throughout their life

819
01:11:08,077 --> 01:11:09,371
and that's how we should be.

820
01:11:09,674 --> 01:11:15,378
But that sometimes is a disease that could come to the heart,

821
01:11:17,243 --> 01:11:20,209
and then Umar said: Then you will live the rest of your life in the state of ignorance.

822
01:11:20,790 --> 01:11:21,839
Learn when you're young.

823
01:11:21,894 --> 01:11:27,331
Plus learning when you're young is better for you

824
01:11:27,432 --> 01:11:29,551
because that's when you have a stronger memory

825
01:11:30,591 --> 01:11:34,005
and memory is very important when it comes to Islamic knowledge

826
01:11:34,678 --> 01:11:39,956
because it depends on memorization. He also said:

827
01:11:40,336 --> 01:11:47,069
يَهْدِيْمُ الْإِسْلَامَ ذَلَّةُ عَالِمٍ وَجَدَالُ مُنَافِقٍ بِالْقُرْآنِ وَ آئِمَّهْ مُزِّلُوْنْ

828
01:11:47,455 --> 01:11:51,983
Islam will be destroyed by a mistake of a scholar,

829
01:11:52,722 --> 01:11:56,401
by the arguments from Qur'an, by a Munafiq(منافق)

830
01:11:56,878 --> 01:12:04,276
and by the misguided Imam(اِمَام)s.

831
01:12:06,263 --> 01:12:11,181
Why do these destroy Islam because people follow their words,

832
01:12:12,525 --> 01:12:14,111
a scholar who makes a mistake.

833
01:12:14,603 --> 01:12:21,070
When Imam Ahmad Bin Humbal(إمام أحمد بن حنبل), was asked to say that Quran was created.

834
01:12:21,094 --> 01:12:23,838
That was the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) that was the Bid'ah(بدعة) of Al-Moa Tazillah(معتزله).

835
01:12:24,280 --> 01:12:27,494
They claim that Quran is not the word of Allah, but it's created.

836
01:12:27,952 --> 01:12:29,776
But that was a very dangerous Bid'ah(بدعة).

837
01:12:30,792 --> 01:12:38,006
Ahmad Bin Humbal رضي الله عنه stood firm and he refused to give in.

838
01:12:39,697 --> 01:12:43,696
In his prison cell, one of the scholars came to him and said;

839
01:12:43,903 --> 01:12:48,898
You are coerced to say that, you are being tortured.

840
01:12:49,724 --> 01:12:54,279
So, you are allowed to speak out publicly, even if you don't believe in it.

841
01:12:54,304 --> 01:12:59,060
Because you are under a state of coercion under duress.

842
01:12:59,234 --> 01:13:01,869
So, you can say that it's created.

843
01:13:03,492 --> 01:13:08,897
Ahmad Bin Humbal(أحمد بن حنبل) pulls the man and he opens the window

844
01:13:09,876 --> 01:13:13,656
and he said: Do you see all of these people, the people of Baghdad(بغداد)? He said: Yes.

845
01:13:14,284 --> 01:13:17,761
He said: If I say that, they will say it too.

846
01:13:19,341 --> 01:13:22,698
People take my word, the people of Baghdad(بغداد) follow what I say.

847
01:13:22,722 --> 01:13:24,696
Not just the people Baghdad(بغداد), but the people of the Muslim world.

848
01:13:25,396 --> 01:13:30,405
If I say it, they will all accept it from me and I know that it's false but they won't,

849
01:13:31,976 --> 01:13:33,666
so he refused to give in.

850
01:13:34,981 --> 01:13:40,929
So, a mistake of a scholar can mislead an Ummah(امة) and

851
01:13:41,079 --> 01:13:43,841
وجدال منافق بالقرآن

852
01:13:44,307 --> 01:13:46,204
A Munafiq(منافق) who has knowledge of Quran

853
01:13:46,244 --> 01:13:49,892
and he's arguing with you using Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an, when he's a Munafiq(منافق),

854
01:13:50,384 --> 01:13:53,443
that's very dangerous because he's using the evidence against you

855
01:13:53,736 --> 01:13:58,101
and he's using Qur'an, so you accept that argument but he's twisting it.

856
01:13:58,516 --> 01:14:01,926
He is playing around with it, He is playing around with the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an.

857
01:14:02,657 --> 01:14:06,077
Munafiq Alaiem Bil Lisaaan(منافق عليهم بلسان) , A Munafiq(منافق) who has a  sweet tongue

858
01:14:09,291 --> 01:14:15,331
and Aaemma Muzilloon(آئمَّه مُزلون), the Imam(اِمَام) is a leader,

859
01:14:15,557 --> 01:14:19,021
Muzilloon(مُزلون) are the ones who deceive others,

860
01:14:19,907 --> 01:14:22,251
so they are Imam(اِمَام)s who deceive the Ummah(امة).

861
01:14:22,291 --> 01:14:28,464
And Imam(اِمَام) here could mean a political leader or a religious leader but maybe it's talking about political leaders

862
01:14:28,775 --> 01:14:31,478
because the Ulema(علماء) are mentioned in the beginning of the statements,

863
01:14:31,511 --> 01:14:35,838
so we would assume that Aimma(آئمه) here is talking about the political leaders,

864
01:14:36,556 --> 01:14:37,644
who deceive others.

865
01:14:38,260 --> 01:14:42,868
So, it's the Imam(اِمَام)s and the Ulema(علماء) who could deceive others

866
01:14:42,941 --> 01:14:46,285
and they are also the ones who benefit the most,

867
01:14:47,371 --> 01:14:50,565
so a person in that position could either benefit a lot or harm a lot.

868
01:14:50,596 --> 01:14:54,523
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

869
01:14:54,772 --> 01:14:58,932
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

870
01:14:58,991 --> 01:15:03,248
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

871
01:15:03,313 --> 01:15:07,469
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

